VPNX integrates with Ruma (https://github.com/RumaTeam/ruma), the emulation frontend of the same team: Ruma lists the tables and starts
VPNX as a runner, and the VPNX splash, applet-mode notice and HOME forwarder are made to look and behave like Ruma's. Ruma itself is a
separate program under its own license; nothing here makes Ruma open source.

This product is built from the following works. Each keeps its own copyright and license; the full texts are in the upstream projects
and, where they are copied here, in the files themselves.

Visual Pinball (https://github.com/vpinball/vpinball)
  The player, renderer, physics and plugins (incl. ScoreView). GPL-3.0-or-later; a few inherited files keep the older "MAME-like"
  license described in its LICENSE. Our changes are patches/vpinball-switch.patch and the files under vpinball/switch/.

PinMAME / libpinmame (https://github.com/vpinball/pinmame)
  BSD-3-Clause for newer files, the inherited "old MAME" license for the rest: free of charge, never sold, and not to be distributed with
  illegal ROM images. Our changes are patches/pinmame-*.patch.

libwinevbs (https://github.com/vpinball/libwinevbs) and Wine
  VBScript. LGPL-2.1-or-later.

bgfx (https://github.com/bkaradzic/bgfx, with the fork used by Visual Pinball) and bgfx.cmake
  BSD-2-Clause; the bgfx.cmake build files are CC0-1.0.

SDL3 (devkitPro port), SDL3_image, SDL3_ttf (https://libsdl.org)
  zlib license.

libzip (https://libzip.org) BSD-3-Clause. FreeImage (toxieainc fork) under its GPLv3 option. FreeType, nlohmann/json: their own licenses.

Mesa NVK and nxvk (https://github.com/PalindromicBreadLoaf/nxvk)
  MIT, with GPL-2.0-or-later parts (compat/nvk_compat.c is GPL-2.0-or-later).

devkitPro, libnx and the switchbrew community
  The toolchain and system library. The forwarder payload in forwarder/ derives from nx-hbloader (ISC, forwarder/LICENSE.md).

Forwarder code (vpinball/switch/forwarder.cpp, forwarder_structs.h)
  Mozilla Public License 2.0, originally from dolphin-nx (https://github.com/NaGaa95/dolphin-nx, Source/Core/DolphinSwitch/), here
  adapted by way of the Ruma frontend, whose forwarder is the same. The MPL requires these two files to keep their notices and their
  source to stay available to whoever receives the NRO.

